What is Crowdfunding?
Crowdfunding represents a disruptive financial model where individuals or organizations raise funds from a large pool of small investors through online platforms. Unlike traditional financing methods, it enables creators to bypass institutional gatekeepers and access capital directly from supporters. First emerging in the UK in 2007, the industry gained mainstream traction through platforms like Kickstarter before expanding globally, with China becoming the dominant market by 2018.
